+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, but Filtering the Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so its provenance stayed open.
+
+A request on 2026-09-18 asked to filter the veterinarian list by specialty. As worded, NG-9 covers that request. The owner decided the row at intake: "free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 as worded.** Rejected by the owner: it declines a filter that repeats no search pattern and adds no new surface to the directory.
+2. **Drop the veterinarian clause from NG-9.** Rejected: it would open free-text veterinarian search, which the owner kept out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 now declines searching for a pet or a visit, and free-text search for a veterinarian. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute the directory already shows is in scope. The specialty filter is the first such filter (`REQ-VET-003`).
+
+Pet and visit search stay declined exactly as before. The owner has not decided those clauses of the row.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The directory can be filtered by specialty on both of its surfaces. A later filter on another shown attribute needs no further change to NG-9.
+- A request for free-text veterinarian search, or for any search over pets or visits, still meets NG-9 and needs its own owner decision.
+- The pet and visit clauses of NG-9 stay part of the open provenance consultation.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-9 row and preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the specialty filter this narrowing admits.
